    "result_text": "All 260 tests pass. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `checkDigit` field on the owner resource as a single Luhn check digit computed over the digits of the `customerCode`.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `checkDigit` property (integer, 0\u20139) to the `Owner` schema, right after `customerCode`. This generates the field into the `OwnerDto`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` binding `checkDigit -> formatCheckDigit(owner)` and a `formatCheckDigit` method that runs the standard Luhn algorithm over the digit characters of the customer code (right-to-left, doubling every other digit, subtracting 9 when >9, then `(10 - sum % 10) % 10`). It returns `null` when the customer code is absent, matching the conventions of the neighboring derived-field mappers.\n\nThis mirrors exactly the `luhn(...)` reference the acceptance test uses, so `AcceptanceTest.coreCheckDigitIsLuhnOfCustomerCode` passes, and the full suite (260 tests) is green.",
